<urn:atm:triage:finding/ARCH-AY-R2-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ARCH-AY-R2-004" ;
  triage:title "O(N^2) doctor --all-teams roster-reload from AY.13 x AY.15 composition" ;
  triage:description "arch-qa quality-gate-r3 verification (PR #1318 fix/ay-gate-r2-schema-docs, head ef79745ae56aaeb62e6f70a91cf4acad2360ee5c). Important. Two independently-correct, independently-tested phase-ay features compose into quadratic cost: (1) AY.13 introduced per-team doctor iteration in load_scoped_rosters (crates/atm-core/src/doctor/team_scope.rs), calling load_member_roster once per team; (2) AY.15 added collision-detection helper push_duplicate_effective_name_warnings in load_member_roster (crates/atm-core/src/doctor/mod.rs:908-940), which unconditionally reloads ALL teams' full rosters on every single call via runtime.list_roster_teams().into_iter().flat_map(...runtime.load_team_roster...) in crates/atm-core/src/doctor/roster_names.rs. Composition result: for N teams, doctor --all-teams now reloads all N teams' rosters N times (once per team, inside the duplicate-warning check). This O(N^2) behavior was invisible to each sprint's own unit-scoped QA. Required correction: hoist the all-teams roster load in load_scoped_rosters to load once, then pass the already-loaded full roster set into push_duplicate_effective_name_warnings (or equivalent single-pass refactor) so the operation scales as O(N) not O(N^2). This impacts doctor --all-teams performance on large team rosters." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ay" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "performance" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "doctor command performance composition" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-08T04:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AY15 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-08T04:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ARCH-AY-R2-004/ARCH-AY-R2-004/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ARCH-AY-R2-004/ARCH-AY-R2-004/2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ARCH-AY-R2-004/ARCH-AY-R2-004/3> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

